{"run_id":"run_5fb0b8204ed5","schema_version":"0.1","seq":11,"t_ms":11,"text":"I couldn't find the actual threshold rules. The notes mention an \"agreed threshold\" but never give a figure or explain how it's applied.\n\n**What the planning variance commentary notes say:**\n- Variance commentary is written against the approved budget.\n- It's reviewed every period.\n- Any material variance above the agreed threshold needs a named owner and a date for fixing it.\n\n**What's missing:** The notes don't say what the threshold is (a percentage, an amount, or both) or who agreed it. The only other document my search found was the \"Finance review calendar 2026,\" which I didn't open. If you know where the threshold is defined, such as a finance policy, I can look it up.","turn":3,"type":"agent.message"}
